body:
Maintainer-apply patch for the rework requested in [the review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/1310#issuecomment-6836947210).

This resolves the module-list conflict by retaining both parents' registrations exactly once, including the newer merge-plan modules/tests, and raises `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` to **46** above the tested main's **45**.

**Tested inputs:** PR head `044df05c3f523560531ef6b54dcaff4492ffb56d` + main `ea8c16bc188e15ff338fbe11a6b621f478828070`. Final resolved tree: `e9b3b71315a0dfc9e6625f148011ea23abe1f1cc`.

**Native Windows validation:** `cargo test -p xtask -- --nocapture`: **109 passed, 0 failed**; five real Cargo directory selections passed **1/1/1/2/1** across three independent fixture outputs. `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed. Final focused `rustfmt --check --edition 2024 --config skip_children=true xtask/src/main.rs`: passed. A separate verifier found no actionable issue in the mechanical resolution. Tests/Clippy ran on tree `cf8fd8a5ec0065ff76e752974a8604e049b85c90`; the final tree differs only by relocating two unchanged `#[cfg(test)]` module declarations as rustfmt required, so that evidence was reused. Application/full/release suites were not run.

From a clean worktree of this PR at the head above, fetch main and start the pinned merge. It is expected to stop at the two conflicts. Save the diff below as `PR1310-maintainer.patch`, then:

```sh
git fetch origin main
git merge --no-commit ea8c16bc188e15ff338fbe11a6b621f478828070
git apply --check PR1310-maintainer.patch
git apply PR1310-maintainer.patch
git add .claude/PROCESS_VERSION xtask/src/main.rs
git write-tree
```

The resulting tree should be `e9b3b71315a0dfc9e6625f148011ea23abe1f1cc`; this exact sequence was verified with the index still unmerged before applying the patch. The maintainer can then commit the merge and update this PR. If integrating a newer main instead, adapt the resolution to that base and set the process version above its current value.

Patch SHA-256: `14b0d925ab1147f74713391e33d4bc12eb8842df7cd879f68c4e9a46f17fe33e`.

